From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] flow: OpenROAD picks the parasitics, the flow says when

The flow decided which parasitics to time with in four places, open.tcl,
generate_abstract.tcl, write_endpoint_slack and final_outputs.tcl, from
the stage number, grt::have_routes and whether a .spef file exists. A
file on disk says nothing about whether it belongs to the design being
timed: re-running a flow from place or global route leaves the previous
final's SPEF in the results directory.

The stage scripts call a bare estimate_parasitics, under log_cmd, where
they want to pay for an estimate, and OpenROAD picks the source (0136).
6_final is timed with 6_final.spef when the final stage extracted it,
which final_extracts_parasitics says from RCX_RULES and
SKIP_DETAILED_ROUTE; read_spef fails if the file is missing. A placed
design is timed with parasitics, a design before placement without.
Subsumes 0135's generate_abstract change, on which it applies.

Not upstreamed yet: a draft ORFS pull request that depends on the
OpenROAD one. Retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS that carries it.
---
